            "merged": true,
            "mergeable": false,
            "draft": false,
            "body": "## Purpose\nFix the T18 demonstrated TOCTOU window: a worker may retain authorization after another worker becomes owner and append twice. Candidate only; **DO NOT MERGE / DO NOT PROMOTE** without independent regression and real sink evidence.\n\n## Scope\n- Fails closed with `SINK_ATOMIC_WRITE_REQUIRED` for unsupported non-idempotent writes.\n- Explicitly limits Sheets writes to one atomic batch creating a unique sheet and writing only that new sheet.\n- Requires deterministic path/version parameters for GitHub create/update.\n- Trusted host write adapters may opt in to sink atomic semantics; they must be separately reviewed.\n- Adds T18/T19 positive/negative tests plus documentation. No stable V2 path changes.\n\n## Evidence\n- Baseline: two independent old-engine unsafe appends caused two provider effects in controlled V8 fixture; historical T18 live test showed 2 matching rows.\n- Candidate V8 execution: 17/17 test callbacks passed; native Node 22 GitHub CI must be independently checked.\n- Real isolated Google Sheets sink-atomic patterns previously passed T19/T20; the new candidate code still needs fresh real connector verification.\n\n## Boundaries\nNo general exactly-once, fencing, lease takeover, or unrestricted arbitrary writes claim. Review potential backward compatibility impact: unguarded historical writes now intentionally BLOCKED. Do not merge main.",
            "title": "Candidate: fail-closed sink-atomic write gate for Legion T18 concurrency regression",
